1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,002
[MODULATED VOICE]
<i>It's time for the whole world to know</i>

2
00:00:03,086 --> 00:00:06,381
<i>that LoveList CEO Billy Cariño</i>
<i>is a criminal.</i>

3
00:00:06,464 --> 00:00:08,591
<i>On June 18, 2013,</i>

4
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:10,385
<i>at 8:30 p.m.,</i>

5
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:13,388
<i>on Feliciano Street, Barangay Del Mundo,</i>

6
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:17,142
<i>she killed Jade Valentin in a hit-and-run.</i>

7
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:20,145
<i>She was the mother</i>
<i>of Billy's friend, Jordan Valentin.</i>

8
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:22,689
<i>I will give you another chance.</i>

9
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:24,774
<i>If you don't follow through,</i>

10
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:26,901
<i>this video will go viral.</i>

11
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:28,236
<i>What's your proof?</i>

12
00:00:28,319 --> 00:00:30,155
<i>I know your company is suffering losses.</i>

13
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:32,032
<i>We all know that.</i>

14
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:34,284
<i>It's all over social media.</i>

15
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:37,579
<i>You know that my company</i>
<i>is suffering losses?</i>

16
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:39,372
<i>Who are you?!</i>

17
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:43,042
<i>You're working with Bea, aren't you?</i>

18
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:45,628
<i>Don't make this conversation</i>
<i>confusing, okay?</i>

19
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:48,548
<i>I want ten million pesos.</i>

20
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,341
<i>I'll give you three days.</i>

21
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,845
[BILLY] <i>Someone's blackmailing me.</i>

22
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:55,972
[JORDAN] <i>Since when?</i>

23
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,016
<i>And why didn't you tell me right away?</i>

24
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:00,185
<i>Because I didn't want</i>
<i>you getting dragged into this.</i>

25
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:03,730
<i>- I don't want you to get hurt.</i>
<i>- Okay. I don't understand.</i>

26
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:05,440
<i>Why would I get hurt?</i>

27
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:09,778
<i>June 18, 2013.</i>

28
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:13,615
<i>She killed Jade Valentin in a hit-and-run.</i>

29
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:15,116
<i>I saw it with my own eyes.</i>

30
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,910
<i>You were the one</i>
<i>who killed her, Billy Cariño!</i>

31
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,536
<i>Who is this bastard?</i>

32
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,997
<i>Why are they using my mom</i>
<i>to ruin your reputation?</i>

33
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:26,044
<i>On the night your mother died…</i>

34
00:01:27,128 --> 00:01:29,464
<i>I was at the same place.</i>

35
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:32,425
<i>That was the night</i>
<i>I rushed my mother to the hospital.</i>

36
00:01:32,509 --> 00:01:33,802
<i>When Oliver was born.</i>

37
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:38,223
<i>The street where your mom was found…</i>

38
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:41,309
<i>I drove down that same street.</i>

39
00:01:41,392 --> 00:01:43,144
<i>Even if you did,</i>

40
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:46,689
<i>you didn't run over anyone, did you?</i>

41
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:49,776
<i>Or else you would've stopped, right?</i>

42
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,279
<i>As far as I know, I didn't.</i>

43
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,949
<i>- I hope I didn't!</i>
<i>- You hope so?</i>

44
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:57,700
<i>I don't remember!</i>

45
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,870
<i>- Sorry!</i>
<i>- No, no.</i>

46
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,122
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

47
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,415
<i>This can't be happening.</i>

48
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:13,341
[BILLY SOBBING]
<i>No! No! No!</i>

49
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:17,011
[SOBBING]

50
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:18,096
[JORDAN] <i>Billy!</i>

51
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:19,472
<i>Billy!</i>

52
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,642
<i>I'm here! It's me, Jordan!</i>

53
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:24,769
<i>Billy.</i>

54
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:27,355
<i>- Come on.</i>
<i>- No! No! No!</i>

55
00:02:27,438 --> 00:02:28,523
<i>No, Jordan! No!</i>

56
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:29,774
<i>- Billy!</i>
<i>- No!</i>

57
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:31,943
<i>Don't come near me!</i>

58
00:02:32,026 --> 00:02:33,736
<i>- No!</i>
<i>- Billy…</i>

59
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,822
<i>- It's okay.</i>
<i>- No! Leave! Leave!</i>

60
00:02:35,905 --> 00:02:37,323
<i>Don't come near me, please!</i>

61
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:38,408
<i>No, no!</i>

62
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:39,534
<i>- No, Jordan.</i>
<i>- Billy…</i>

63
00:02:39,617 --> 00:02:40,702
<i>- No…</i>
<i>- It's okay.</i>

64
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:42,579
[BILLY CRYING]

65
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:43,705
<i>Let's go home.</i>

66
00:02:44,497 --> 00:02:45,957
<i>- No!</i>
<i>- Come on.</i>

67
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,792
<i>Leave! Please!</i>

68
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:50,962
<i>Please go away, Jordan! Please!</i>

69
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:53,214
<i>It's okay.</i>

70
00:02:53,298 --> 00:03:00,305
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:01,449
Billy…

72
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:08,748
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:04:08,831 --> 00:04:09,958
We'll get through this.

74
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,042
[BILLY BREATHES HEAVILY]

75
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,210
Together.

76
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:15,630
All right, get some rest.

77
00:04:15,713 --> 00:04:17,006
I'll get going.

78
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:21,678
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:04:31,729 --> 00:04:32,772
Bea.

80
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,734
Wow. You really went to all that trouble.

81
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:42,240
Jordan, I have nothing to do with
whoever is blackmailing Billy.

82
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:44,575
Just think about it, okay? I wasn't there.

83
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:47,912
<i>I don't even know how your mother died.</i>

84
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:50,415
You're the only one
who has a grudge against Billy.

85
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:52,917
You're the only one who has the motive.

86
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:55,420
We know what you're capable of, Bea.

87
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,422
And the details are online.

88
00:04:57,505 --> 00:04:59,299
Jordan, I'm no longer mad at Billy.

89
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,009
I'm fine now. I'm not mad anymore.

90
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:03,344
- If it wasn't you, then who?
- I don't know!

91
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:04,762
I don't know!

92
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:07,223
Maybe they're not actually
targeting Billy at all.

93
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:09,267
Maybe someone's just using
Billy against you.

94
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:10,768
Think about that too.

95
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:17,483
[RAIN DRIZZLING]

96
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:22,530
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:42,717
What happened to you?

98
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:47,013
Why do you seem sad?

99
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:54,312
I'm just tired.

100
00:05:58,441 --> 00:05:59,609
Are you okay?

101
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:02,361
[RAIN DRIZZLING]

102
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:14,123
I used to think

103
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:18,169
that if you were a good person,

104
00:06:18,252 --> 00:06:20,296
life would be easy.

105
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,636
Because you do the right thing.

106
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:34,727
But being a good person is actually hard.

107
00:06:36,896 --> 00:06:40,441
Especially when the world
isn't good to you either.

108
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:44,529
["AKO NAMAN MUNA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

109
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:45,780
So, yeah.

110
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:49,617
I got tired.

111
00:06:51,202 --> 00:06:53,162
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

112
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:55,123
I got tired of trusting people.

113
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:00,962
What else did you do?

114
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:07,552
I got angry.

115
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:12,265
I pushed them all away.

116
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:15,643
Everyone?

117
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:18,729
Everyone.

118
00:07:21,107 --> 00:07:22,650
Our family.

119
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:25,278
My friends.

120
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:29,031
Jordan.

121
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:35,037
Even myself.

122
00:07:35,121 --> 00:07:39,750
["AKO NAMAN MUNA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

123
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:45,923
I feel like I'm all alone.

124
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:51,971
You felt they left you…

125
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:57,560
just like how we were left before?

126
00:07:57,643 --> 00:08:02,273
["AKO NAMAN MUNA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

127
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:12,617
But you know what I learned from all this?

128
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:18,289
It's that some people will leave

129
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:21,334
and others will come into our lives.

130
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:28,257
But there are also people
who'll stay with us.

131
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:35,306
["AKO NAMAN MUNA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

132
00:08:36,516 --> 00:08:39,936
There are people who won't
give up on us even when…

133
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:43,064
we've made mistakes.

134
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:45,024
[BREATH QUIVERS]

135
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,528
And even when we're no longer lovable.

136
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:49,820
Really?

137
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:56,494
[RAIN PATTERING]

138
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:57,703
[SIGHS]

139
00:08:57,787 --> 00:08:58,913
So…

140
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,124
you're not mad anymore?

141
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:05,711
[RAIN PATTERING]

142
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:12,426
["AKO NAMAN MUNA"
BY ANGELA KEN PLAYING]

143
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:18,015
[CRYING] I'm done being mad.

144
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:26,023
- ["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]
- [CRYING] I'm done.

145
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,818
I'm still here.

146
00:09:28,901 --> 00:09:31,612
[CRYING]

147
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,948
Even if you lose everything,

148
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:37,285
I will never leave you.

149
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:39,829
[SOBS SOFTLY]

150
00:09:41,539 --> 00:09:48,212
Just come back to me whenever
you feel that anger building up again.

151
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:53,092
Or when you feel tired.

152
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:58,014
I hope you'll remember me…

153
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:02,643
because I'm always here.

154
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:06,439
[SNIFFLES]

155
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:09,650
[CRYING]

156
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:13,613
Even when I'm hard to love?

157
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:18,200
Especially when you're hard to love.

158
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:23,581
["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]

159
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:31,589
I thought I could do it on my own.

160
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:41,307
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you.

161
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:48,105
["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]

162
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,320
It's okay.

163
00:10:55,446 --> 00:10:56,280
[BILLY SOBS]

164
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:58,032
What's important

165
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:00,409
is that you're here.

166
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:01,577
[SOBS]

167
00:11:03,746 --> 00:11:06,666
I promise, from now on,

168
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:13,130
I'll take care of you and protect you.

169
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:19,762
I won't leave you again.

170
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:25,226
And I won't leave either.

171
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:39,115
- ["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]
- [RAIN PATTERING]

172
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:06,350
- ["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]
- [RAIN PATTERING]

173
00:12:25,077 --> 00:12:31,000
["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]

174
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:33,085
[SOBS]

175
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:57,651
["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]

176
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,577
[SNIFFLES]

177
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:18,839
["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]

178
00:13:40,778 --> 00:13:41,820
Hm?

179
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,324
[BILLY SNIFFLES, SOBS]

180
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:51,705
[BILLY SNIFFLES]

181
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:55,376
["AKO NAMAN MUNA" CONTINUES]

182
00:13:55,459 --> 00:14:00,839
[SOBBING]

183
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:14,103
I miss my daughter.

184
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:16,981
[JUDE] My daughter, Jade.

185
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:20,276
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:23,112
We used to play the guitar
all the time back then too.

187
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:25,865
[CHUCKLES] And then…

188
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:31,078
And then a lot of people would tip us.

189
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:33,747
[CHUCKLES] It's because my daughter

190
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:38,586
is an excellent singer and guitarist.

191
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:44,884
[LAUGHING]

192
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,679
I miss her too, Grandpa.

193
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:51,891
So much.

194
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:56,604
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:58,147
[JORDAN] All these years…

196
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,359
and justice still hasn't been served.

197
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,070
What if…

198
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,490
that fact is really difficult to accept?

199
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:16,081
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

200
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:41,565
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:06,173
[NECKLACE CLINKS]

202
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:11,762
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

203
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:18,102
[JUDE] <i>Why did you punch him?</i>
<i>You should've just let it slide.</i>

204
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:19,687
They were teasing me!

205
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,856
<i>They said I'd fail to get</i>
<i>into computer engineering.</i>

206
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,775
[JUDE]<i> Once your mother</i>
<i>finds out about this,</i>

207
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:25,901
<i>she will be furious again.</i>

208
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,695
<i>Well, I have a peace offering.</i>

209
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:31,365
<i>Wow, you even have a bribe.</i>

210
00:16:31,448 --> 00:16:33,367
[LAUGHTER]

211
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:34,827
<i>Look at this kid!</i>

212
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:36,161
[CHUCKLES]

213
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:43,836
<i>Jade?</i>

214
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:46,547
<i>Jade!</i>

215
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:47,923
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Mommy!</i>

216
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:48,966
<i>Mommy!</i>

217
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:51,468
[CRYING] <i>Mommy!</i>

218
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:55,889
[SOBBING] <i>Mommy!</i>

219
00:16:56,598 --> 00:17:00,102
- [YOUNG JORDAN SOBBING]
<i>- Help! Help!</i>

220
00:17:00,185 --> 00:17:02,312
<i>Anyone! Help us!</i>

221
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:06,900
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

222
00:17:07,526 --> 00:17:09,153
[DINO GROANS IN PAIN]

223
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:11,447
<i>Good thing the bullet just grazed him.</i>

224
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:13,282
<i>Do we need to take him to the hospital?</i>

225
00:17:13,907 --> 00:17:15,993
<i>No, no. I can't go to the hospital.</i>

226
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:17,619
<i>Good to know,</i>

227
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:20,622
<i>because I have to go somewhere.</i>

228
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:22,207
<i>Take care of your father for now, okay?</i>

229
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:23,751
<i>I'll go ahead.</i>

230
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,502
[DINO] <i>Thank you, son.</i>

231
00:17:27,963 --> 00:17:29,298
<i>I'll be back, okay? I'll be quick.</i>

232
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:30,382
<i>Wait.</i>

233
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,720
<i>That necklace belonged to my mom.</i>

234
00:17:36,805 --> 00:17:39,099
<i>This is mine. Your father gave it to me.</i>

235
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:44,396
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:17:56,950 --> 00:18:01,955
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:09,171
<i>Jordan, uh…</i>

238
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:13,967
<i>I can't change what happened in the past.</i>

239
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:17,554
<i>I regret it all.</i>

240
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:21,308
<i>But if</i>

241
00:18:21,391 --> 00:18:26,188
<i>you'll let me prove to you</i>
<i>that I've changed,</i>

242
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:27,898
<i>I want to make it up to you.</i>

243
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:32,903
<i>If you'll give me a chance,</i>
<i>I'm going to change for the better.</i>

244
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:39,660
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:51,463
[CELL PHONE RINGING]

246
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:54,967
Dude?

247
00:18:57,636 --> 00:19:02,182
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,608
[BOTTLE THUDS]

249
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:17,865
[JORDAN SIGHS]

250
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:20,117
[BILLY] Dude.

251
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:28,500
[MUSIC FADES]

252
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:33,213
I said I'd come to you.

253
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:35,340
Are you feeling better now?

254
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:39,469
Yeah.

255
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,472
Thank you.

256
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:47,728
What did you want to tell me?

257
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:51,064
This necklace…

258
00:19:53,775 --> 00:19:56,486
My mom was wearing it
the last time I saw her.

259
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:57,905
The day she died.

260
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:03,327
But it ended up with Karen,
my dad's partner.

261
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:09,416
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:14,838
Billy, look.

263
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:18,800
She's the one in the video.
That's Karen, not Bea.

264
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:20,636
I remember that dress.

265
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:24,264
[MUSIC BECOMES STIRRING]

266
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:26,225
S-So, this means…

267
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:28,685
I can't say for sure

268
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:31,521
if Dad had anything to do with
what happened to Mom.

269
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:33,982
But if that's really her necklace,

270
00:20:35,859 --> 00:20:37,402
how did it end up with Karen?

271
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:41,448
[JORDAN SIGHS]

272
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,700
I need to hear the truth from him

273
00:20:44,743 --> 00:20:48,080
so we can prove your innocence.

274
00:20:50,374 --> 00:20:52,542
And for your mother, Jordan.

275
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:57,506
So that we can get justice for her death.

276
00:20:58,131 --> 00:21:03,804
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

277
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:08,850
What's your plan?

278
00:21:11,144 --> 00:21:12,813
I'll think of something.

279
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:15,065
I'll come with you.

280
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:20,696
Wait, are you sure?

281
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:24,700
[JORDAN SIGHS]

282
00:21:24,783 --> 00:21:28,870
I know it's not easy
having to relive that night.

283
00:21:30,872 --> 00:21:32,040
Will you be okay?

284
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:35,711
I'm not going to leave you.

285
00:21:42,759 --> 00:21:44,386
I also talked to Bea.

286
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:47,180
She denied involvement with
whoever is blackmailing you.

287
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:50,017
[JORDAN SIGHS]

288
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:51,893
I think she's telling the truth.

289
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:59,276
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:07,367
<i>Thank you for putting up with me.</i>

291
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:10,954
<i>LoveList isn't just a company.</i>

292
00:22:11,038 --> 00:22:12,122
<i>We all know that.</i>

293
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:16,460
<i>We worked hard for this.</i>
<i>This is our family.</i>

294
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:19,546
<i>Billy,</i>

295
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:21,006
<i>I just wanted to make it clear</i>

296
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:24,676
<i>that I have nothing to do with</i>
<i>the blackmail you're getting.</i>

297
00:22:25,761 --> 00:22:27,429
<i>I came here because…</i>

298
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:30,474
<i>I want to help.</i>

299
00:22:30,557 --> 00:22:33,935
<i>I know that I've done you</i>
<i>and LoveList wrong.</i>

300
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:36,104
<i>I'm not denying that.</i>

301
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:38,440
<i>But I swear, this one isn't on me.</i>

302
00:22:38,523 --> 00:22:40,400
<i>I just want to help.</i>

303
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:41,860
<i>You want to help me?</i>

304
00:22:41,943 --> 00:22:45,530
<i>Yes. I'll do anything. Just tell me.</i>

305
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:47,908
<i>Wow!</i>

306
00:22:47,991 --> 00:22:50,619
<i>Let's give this liar a round of applause!</i>

307
00:22:50,702 --> 00:22:51,787
[APPLAUSE]

308
00:22:51,870 --> 00:22:53,371
<i>Great acting!</i>

309
00:22:53,455 --> 00:22:55,957
<i>Meet me tomorrow night</i>

310
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:59,211
<i>at ten o'clock on Gerona Avenue.</i>

311
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:00,962
<i>Bring 10 million pesos.</i>

312
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:04,633
<i>Don't even think about</i>
<i>bringing the police.</i>

313
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:11,556
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
